TableDefinition: One table's schema contract.

FIELDS:
- table (string): Table name
- columns (array): Column defs
- primary_key (string): PK column
- engine (string): Storage engine

EXAMPLE:
{
 "table": "orders",
 "columns": [
  {
   "name": "id",
   "type": "uuid"
  },
  {
   "name": "total",
   "type": "numeric"
  }
 ],
 "primary_key": "id",
 "engine": "innodb"
}

STANDARD: Relational conventions. Every record of this type should carry these fields with these meanings — that consistency is what makes data interoperable across database architecture systems.

